module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Constructions.EpiMono
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Preserves.Finite
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.InternalEndFunctor
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.MonObjImagePoint

/-!
# A monoidal exact functor and the image of a point of a monoid object

Let `𝒜` and `ℬ` be abelian braided monoidal closed categories, let `F : 𝒜 ⥤ ℬ` be a lax monoidal
exact functor, let `C` be a monoid object of `𝒜` and let `p : 𝟙_ 𝒜 ⟶ C.X` be a point of it.
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.MonObjImagePoint` builds from this data the subobject
`p * C = Limits.image (CategoryTheory.Mon.leftMul C p)` of `C.X`, the right action
`CategoryTheory.Mon.imageActionRight` of `C` on it, and the resulting morphism of monoid objects
`CategoryTheory.Mon.imageRep C p : C ⟶ MonoidalClosed.internalEnd (p * C)`. This file transports
all of that along `F`.

The transported point is `CategoryTheory.Mon.mapPoint F p`, a point of the monoid object
`F.mapMon.obj C`. Left multiplication by it is the image under `F` of left multiplication by `p`,
so exactness of `F` identifies `F (p * C)` with `(F p) * (F C)`; under that identification the
right action and the representation are the images of the right action and the representation of
`C`. The conclusion is that the representation of `F.mapMon.obj C` on the image of left
multiplication by `mapPoint F p` is invertible exactly when `F.mapMon` carries
`Mon.imageRep C p` to an isomorphism.

For the pullback of sheaves of modules along a morphism of schemes this says that the pullback of
the subsheaf generated by a global section is the subsheaf generated by the pulled-back section,
and that the pullback of the associated endomorphism-algebra representation is the one of the
pullback.

## Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.Limits.imageIsoOfMapEq`: a functor preserving finite limits and colimits
  between abelian categories carries the image of `u` to the image of any morphism equal to
  `F.map u`.
* `CategoryTheory.Mon.mapPoint`: the point of `F.mapMon.obj C` induced by a point of `C`.
* `CategoryTheory.Mon.mapImageLeftMulIso`: **`F` carries the subobject `p * C` to the subobject
  `(mapPoint F p) * (F.mapMon.obj C)`.**

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.curry_comp_ihomFunctorComparison`: the currying rule for the
  internal-hom comparison of a lax monoidal functor, and
  `CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.curry_comp_internalEndCongrHom` the currying rule for
  conjugation by an isomorphism. These are the two computation rules the main result runs on.
* `CategoryTheory.Mon.map_leftMul` and `CategoryTheory.Mon.map_rightMul`: **a lax monoidal
  functor carries left (resp. right) multiplication by a point to left (resp. right)
  multiplication by the transported point.**
* `CategoryTheory.Mon.comp_imageActionRight_of_comp_ι`,
  `CategoryTheory.Mon.imageActionRight_eq_of_comp_ι` and
  `CategoryTheory.Mon.eq_imageActionRight_of_comp_ι`: a morphism to `p * C` restricting the
  multiplication of `C` intertwines any action with `Mon.imageActionRight`. This is the
  characterisation of the right action that the transport is deduced from.
* `CategoryTheory.Mon.map_imageActionRight`: **the right action is preserved.**
* `CategoryTheory.Mon.mapMon_imageRep`: **the main result — a lax monoidal exact functor
  commutes with the representation of a monoid object on the image of left multiplication by a
  point.**
* `CategoryTheory.Mon.isIso_mapMon_imageRep_iff`: for a braided monoidal exact functor and a
  dualizable `p * C`, the transported representation is invertible exactly when the image of the
  representation is.

## Implementation notes

Every statement is made with the weakest hypotheses it needs, and these differ a lot across the
file: the two currying rules need only lax monoidality, the characterisation lemmas need no
functor at all, the image comparison needs exactness but neither a braiding nor closedness, the
main result needs all of abelian, braided, closed and exact on both sides but only lax
monoidality, and only the final `isIso` criterion needs `F` braided monoidal with `p * C`
dualizable — that hypothesis enters solely through
`CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.isIso_internalEndFunctorHom`, which is where the symmetry of the
two categories is used as well.

`(F.mapMon.obj C).X` is only *definitionally* `F.obj C.X`: unfolding
`CategoryTheory.Functor.mapMon` is needed, so the two are not interchangeable at reducible
transparency. A statement mixing them — and the transport statements all do, because
`Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ F H C.X` is typed with `F.obj C.X` while
`Mon.imageActionRight (F.mapMon.obj C) q` is typed with `(F.mapMon.obj C).X` — elaborates, but `rw`
and `simp` cannot act on it, since the motive they build is rejected. Hence the shape of this file:
the computational content is isolated in lemmas stated about variables, where no such mixing
occurs, and the transport statements are obtained from those by application, which unifies at
default transparency. `Mon.map_leftMul` and `Mon.map_rightMul` instead open with a `change` that
moves the goal into the `F.obj C.X` spelling, which is the same device.

Everything is built on `Mon.leftMul` and `Mon.imageActionRight`, i.e. on the *right* action,
because that is the side that represents into `MonoidalClosed.internalEnd`; see the
implementation notes of `StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.MonObjImagePoint`.

`Limits.imageIsoOfMapEq` is `CategoryTheory.PreservesImage.iso` with a twist: it compares
`F (image u)` with the image of a morphism merely *equal* to `F.map u`, rather than with the
image of `F.map u` itself. The twist is the point — it is what lets
`Mon.mapImageLeftMulIso` land on the image of left multiplication by the transported point with
no transport of structure along an equality of objects.
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory Limits MonoidalClosed
open scoped MonObj CategoryTheory.Obj

namespace CategoryTheory.Limits

variable {𝒜 : Type*} {ℬ : Type*} [Category 𝒜] [Category ℬ] [Abelian 𝒜] [Abelian ℬ]
  (F : 𝒜 ⥤ ℬ) [PreservesFiniteLimits F] [PreservesFiniteColimits F]
  {A B : 𝒜} {u : A ⟶ B} {v : F.obj A ⟶ F.obj B}

/-- **An exact functor between abelian categories carries the image of `u` to the image of any
morphism equal to `F.map u`.** The epi-mono factorisation of `u` is carried to an epi-mono
factorisation of `F.map u`, and in an abelian category that is the image factorisation. -/
noncomputable def imageIsoOfMapEq (h : F.map u = v) : F.obj (image u) ≅ image v :=
  letI := strongEpi_of_epi (F.map (factorThruImage u))
  image.isoStrongEpiMono (F.map (factorThruImage u)) (F.map (image.ι u))
    (by rw [← F.map_comp, image.fac, h])

/-- The comparison of the two images is compatible with the two image inclusions. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem imageIsoOfMapEq_hom_comp_ι (h : F.map u = v) :
    (imageIsoOfMapEq F h).hom ≫ image.ι v = F.map (image.ι u) :=
  let := strongEpi_of_epi (F.map (factorThruImage u))
  image.isoStrongEpiMono_hom_comp_ι _ _ _

/-- The comparison of the two images is compatible with the two factorisations through the
image. Together with `CategoryTheory.Limits.imageIsoOfMapEq_hom_comp_ι` this characterises it. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem map_factorThruImage_comp_imageIsoOfMapEq_hom (h : F.map u = v) :
    F.map (factorThruImage u) ≫ (imageIsoOfMapEq F h).hom = factorThruImage v := by
  rw [← cancel_mono (image.ι v), Category.assoc, imageIsoOfMapEq_hom_comp_ι, ← F.map_comp,
    image.fac, image.fac, h]

end CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed

variable {𝒜 : Type*} {ℬ : Type*} [Category 𝒜] [Category ℬ] [MonoidalCategory 𝒜]
  [MonoidalCategory ℬ] [MonoidalClosed 𝒜] [MonoidalClosed ℬ]

/-- **The currying rule for the internal-hom comparison of a lax monoidal functor**: the image
under `F` of a curried morphism, followed by the comparison, is the curried form of the
tensorator followed by the image of that morphism. Only lax monoidality is used. -/
theorem curry_comp_ihomFunctorComparison (F : 𝒜 ⥤ ℬ) [F.LaxMonoidal] {X Y Z : 𝒜}
    (g : X ⊗ Z ⟶ Y) :
    F.map (MonoidalClosed.curry g) ≫ MonoidalClosed.ihomFunctorComparison F X Y =
      MonoidalClosed.curry (Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ F X Z ≫ F.map g) := by
  apply uncurry_injective
  rw [uncurry_natural_left, uncurry_ihomFunctorComparison,
    Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ_natural_right_assoc, ← Functor.map_comp, ← uncurry_eq,
    uncurry_curry, uncurry_curry]

/-- **The currying rule for conjugation of internal endomorphisms by an isomorphism**: composing
a curried morphism with `CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.internalEndCongrHom` conjugates the
morphism itself. -/
theorem curry_comp_internalEndCongrHom {X Y Z : 𝒜} (e : X ≅ Y) (g : X ⊗ Z ⟶ X) :
    curry g ≫ internalEndCongrHom e = curry ((e.inv ⊗ₘ 𝟙 Z) ≫ g ≫ e.hom) := by
  apply uncurry_injective
  rw [uncurry_natural_left, uncurry_internalEndCongrHom, whisker_exchange_assoc,
    whiskerLeft_curry_ihom_ev_app_assoc, uncurry_curry, tensorHom_id]

end CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed

namespace CategoryTheory.Mon

/-! ### Multiplication by a point is preserved -/

section Monoidal

variable {𝒜 : Type*} {ℬ : Type*} [Category 𝒜] [Category ℬ] [MonoidalCategory 𝒜]
  [MonoidalCategory ℬ] (F : 𝒜 ⥤ ℬ) [F.LaxMonoidal] {C : Mon 𝒜} (p : 𝟙_ 𝒜 ⟶ C.X)

/-- The point of `F.mapMon.obj C` induced by a point `p` of a monoid object `C` of `𝒜`: the unit
of the lax monoidal functor `F` followed by the image of `p`. -/
def mapPoint : 𝟙_ ℬ ⟶ (F.mapMon.obj C).X := Functor.LaxMonoidal.ε F ≫ F.map p

/-- **A lax monoidal functor carries left multiplication by a point to left multiplication by the
transported point.** -/
theorem map_leftMul : F.map (leftMul C p) = leftMul (F.mapMon.obj C) (mapPoint F p) := by
  change F.map ((λ_ C.X).inv ≫ (p ▷ C.X) ≫ μ[C.X]) =
    (λ_ (F.obj C.X)).inv ≫ ((Functor.LaxMonoidal.ε F ≫ F.map p) ▷ F.obj C.X) ≫
      (Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ F C.X C.X ≫ F.map μ[C.X])
  rw [comp_whiskerRight, Category.assoc, Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ_natural_left_assoc,
    Functor.LaxMonoidal.left_unitality_inv_assoc, Functor.map_comp, Functor.map_comp]

/-- **A lax monoidal functor carries right multiplication by a point to right multiplication by
the transported point.** -/
theorem map_rightMul : F.map (rightMul C p) = rightMul (F.mapMon.obj C) (mapPoint F p) := by
  change F.map ((ρ_ C.X).inv ≫ (C.X ◁ p) ≫ μ[C.X]) =
    (ρ_ (F.obj C.X)).inv ≫ (F.obj C.X ◁ (Functor.LaxMonoidal.ε F ≫ F.map p)) ≫
      (Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ F C.X C.X ≫ F.map μ[C.X])
  rw [MonoidalCategory.whiskerLeft_comp, Category.assoc,
    Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ_natural_right_assoc,
    Functor.LaxMonoidal.right_unitality_inv_assoc, Functor.map_comp, Functor.map_comp]

end Monoidal

/-! ### The right action on the image of left multiplication, characterised -/

section Characterisation

variable {𝒜 : Type*} [Category 𝒜] [MonoidalCategory 𝒜] [Abelian 𝒜] [BraidedCategory 𝒜]
  [MonoidalClosed 𝒜] (C : Mon 𝒜) (p : 𝟙_ 𝒜 ⟶ C.X) {W : 𝒜} (n : W ⟶ C.X) (a : W ⊗ C.X ⟶ W)

/-- **The right action of `C` on `p * C` is characterised by the restriction of the
multiplication of `C`**: if `w : W ⟶ p * C` is a morphism whose composite with the image
inclusion is `n`, and if an endomorphism-like `a : W ⊗ C.X ⟶ W` restricts the multiplication of
`C` along `n`, then `w` intertwines `a` with `CategoryTheory.Mon.imageActionRight`. -/
theorem comp_imageActionRight_of_comp_ι (w : W ⟶ image (leftMul C p))
    (hw : w ≫ image.ι (leftMul C p) = n) (ha : a ≫ n = (n ▷ C.X) ≫ μ[C.X]) :
    a ≫ w = (w ⊗ₘ 𝟙 C.X) ≫ imageActionRight C p := by
  rw [← cancel_mono (image.ι (leftMul C p)), Category.assoc, hw, ha, Category.assoc,
    imageActionRight_comp_ι, tensorHom_id, ← comp_whiskerRight_assoc, hw]

/-- The characterisation of the right action of `C` on `p * C`, for an isomorphism `w`: the
action is the conjugate of `a`. -/
theorem imageActionRight_eq_of_comp_ι (w : W ≅ image (leftMul C p))
    (hw : w.hom ≫ image.ι (leftMul C p) = n) (ha : a ≫ n = (n ▷ C.X) ≫ μ[C.X]) :
    (w.inv ⊗ₘ 𝟙 C.X) ≫ a ≫ w.hom = imageActionRight C p := by
  rw [comp_imageActionRight_of_comp_ι C p n a w.hom hw ha, tensorHom_id, tensorHom_id,
    ← comp_whiskerRight_assoc, w.inv_hom_id, id_whiskerRight, Category.id_comp]

/-- The characterisation of the right action of `C` on `p * C`, for an isomorphism `w`, read as a
formula for `a`. -/
theorem eq_imageActionRight_of_comp_ι (w : W ≅ image (leftMul C p))
    (hw : w.hom ≫ image.ι (leftMul C p) = n) (ha : a ≫ n = (n ▷ C.X) ≫ μ[C.X]) :
    a = (w.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 C.X) ≫ imageActionRight C p ≫ w.inv := by
  rw [← imageActionRight_eq_of_comp_ι C p n a w hw ha]
  simp

end Characterisation

/-! ### The subobject, the action and the representation are preserved -/

section Exact

variable {𝒜 : Type*} {ℬ : Type*} [Category 𝒜] [Category ℬ] [MonoidalCategory 𝒜]
  [MonoidalCategory ℬ] (F : 𝒜 ⥤ ℬ) [F.LaxMonoidal] [Abelian 𝒜] [Abelian ℬ]
  [PreservesFiniteLimits F] [PreservesFiniteColimits F] {C : Mon 𝒜} (p : 𝟙_ 𝒜 ⟶ C.X)

/-- **An exact lax monoidal functor carries the subobject `p * C` of `C.X` to the subobject
`(mapPoint F p) * (F.mapMon.obj C)` of `F.obj C.X`.** Neither a braiding nor closedness is
needed: this is only the statement that `F` preserves the image of left multiplication, which by
`CategoryTheory.Mon.map_leftMul` is left multiplication by the transported point. -/
noncomputable def mapImageLeftMulIso :
    F.obj (image (leftMul C p)) ≅ image (leftMul (F.mapMon.obj C) (mapPoint F p)) :=
  imageIsoOfMapEq F (map_leftMul F p)

/-- The comparison of the two subobjects is compatible with the two image inclusions. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem mapImageLeftMulIso_hom_comp_ι :
    (mapImageLeftMulIso F p).hom ≫ image.ι (leftMul (F.mapMon.obj C) (mapPoint F p)) =
      F.map (image.ι (leftMul C p)) :=
  imageIsoOfMapEq_hom_comp_ι F (map_leftMul F p)

/-- The comparison of the two subobjects is compatible with the two factorisations through the
image. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem map_factorThruImage_comp_mapImageLeftMulIso_hom :
    F.map (factorThruImage (leftMul C p)) ≫ (mapImageLeftMulIso F p).hom =
      factorThruImage (leftMul (F.mapMon.obj C) (mapPoint F p)) :=
  map_factorThruImage_comp_imageIsoOfMapEq_hom F (map_leftMul F p)

section Braided

variable [BraidedCategory 𝒜] [MonoidalClosed 𝒜] [MonoidalClosed ℬ]

omit [Abelian ℬ] [PreservesFiniteLimits F] [PreservesFiniteColimits F] [MonoidalClosed ℬ] in
/-- The tensorator followed by the image of the right action of `C` on `p * C` restricts the
multiplication of `F.mapMon.obj C` along the image of the inclusion of `p * C`. This is the
hypothesis `CategoryTheory.Mon.eq_imageActionRight_of_comp_ι` needs, in the spelling that avoids
`(F.mapMon.obj C).X`. -/
theorem map_imageActionRight_comp_map_ι :
    (Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ F (image (leftMul C p)) C.X ≫ F.map (imageActionRight C p)) ≫
        F.map (image.ι (leftMul C p)) =
      (F.map (image.ι (leftMul C p)) ▷ F.obj C.X) ≫
        Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ F C.X C.X ≫ F.map μ[C.X] := by
  rw [Category.assoc, ← F.map_comp, imageActionRight_comp_ι, F.map_comp,
    ← Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ_natural_left_assoc]

variable [BraidedCategory ℬ]

/-- **The right action of a monoid object on the image of left multiplication by a point is
preserved by an exact lax monoidal functor**: the tensorator followed by the image of the action
is the action of `F.mapMon.obj C` on the image of left multiplication by the transported point,
conjugated by `CategoryTheory.Mon.mapImageLeftMulIso`. -/
theorem map_imageActionRight :
    Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ F (image (leftMul C p)) C.X ≫ F.map (imageActionRight C p) =
      ((mapImageLeftMulIso F p).hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 (F.mapMon.obj C).X) ≫
        imageActionRight (F.mapMon.obj C) (mapPoint F p) ≫ (mapImageLeftMulIso F p).inv :=
  eq_imageActionRight_of_comp_ι (F.mapMon.obj C) (mapPoint F p)
    (F.map (image.ι (leftMul C p))) _ (mapImageLeftMulIso F p)
    (mapImageLeftMulIso_hom_comp_ι F p) (map_imageActionRight_comp_map_ι F p)

/-- The transported right action, read off from the right action of `C` on `p * C`. This is
`CategoryTheory.Mon.map_imageActionRight` solved for the transported action. -/
theorem imageActionRight_mapPoint_eq :
    ((mapImageLeftMulIso F p).inv ⊗ₘ 𝟙 (F.mapMon.obj C).X) ≫
        (Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ F (image (leftMul C p)) C.X ≫ F.map (imageActionRight C p)) ≫
          (mapImageLeftMulIso F p).hom =
      imageActionRight (F.mapMon.obj C) (mapPoint F p) :=
  imageActionRight_eq_of_comp_ι (F.mapMon.obj C) (mapPoint F p)
    (F.map (image.ι (leftMul C p))) _ (mapImageLeftMulIso F p)
    (mapImageLeftMulIso_hom_comp_ι F p) (map_imageActionRight_comp_map_ι F p)

omit [BraidedCategory ℬ] in
/-- The underlying morphism of the main result: the image of the curried right action, followed
by the internal-hom comparison and by conjugation along
`CategoryTheory.Mon.mapImageLeftMulIso`, is the curried conjugate of the tensorator followed by
the image of the right action. This is the two currying rules, and nothing else. -/
theorem map_imageRepHom_comp :
    F.map (curry (imageActionRight C p)) ≫
        ihomFunctorComparison F (image (leftMul C p)) (image (leftMul C p)) ≫
        internalEndCongrHom (mapImageLeftMulIso F p) =
      curry (((mapImageLeftMulIso F p).inv ⊗ₘ 𝟙 (F.obj C.X)) ≫
        (Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ F (image (leftMul C p)) C.X ≫ F.map (imageActionRight C p)) ≫
          (mapImageLeftMulIso F p).hom) := by
  rw [← Category.assoc, curry_comp_ihomFunctorComparison, curry_comp_internalEndCongrHom]

/-- **A lax monoidal exact functor commutes with the representation of a monoid object on the
image of left multiplication by a point.** The image under `F.mapMon` of
`CategoryTheory.Mon.imageRep C p`, followed by the internal-hom comparison of `F` and by
conjugation along `CategoryTheory.Mon.mapImageLeftMulIso`, is the representation of
`F.mapMon.obj C` on the image of left multiplication by the transported point.

No duality and no braiding of `F` is needed; those enter only in
`CategoryTheory.Mon.isIso_mapMon_imageRep_iff`, to make the two other factors invertible. -/
theorem mapMon_imageRep :
    F.mapMon.map (imageRep C p) ≫
        MonoidalClosed.internalEndFunctorHom F (image (leftMul C p)) ≫
        (MonoidalClosed.internalEndCongr (mapImageLeftMulIso F p)).hom =
      imageRep (F.mapMon.obj C) (mapPoint F p) :=
  Mon.Hom.ext' ((map_imageRepHom_comp F p).trans
    (congrArg MonoidalClosed.curry (imageActionRight_mapPoint_eq F p)))

end Braided

end Exact

section Dual

variable {𝒜 : Type*} {ℬ : Type*} [Category 𝒜] [Category ℬ] [MonoidalCategory 𝒜]
  [MonoidalCategory ℬ] [SymmetricCategory 𝒜] [SymmetricCategory ℬ] [MonoidalClosed 𝒜]
  [MonoidalClosed ℬ] [Abelian 𝒜] [Abelian ℬ] (F : 𝒜 ⥤ ℬ) [F.Braided]
  [PreservesFiniteLimits F] [PreservesFiniteColimits F] {C : Mon 𝒜} (p : 𝟙_ 𝒜 ⟶ C.X)

/-- **For a braided monoidal exact functor and a dualizable `p * C`, the representation of
`F.mapMon.obj C` on the image of left multiplication by the transported point is invertible
exactly when `F.mapMon` carries the representation of `C` on `p * C` to an isomorphism.** The two
remaining factors of `CategoryTheory.Mon.mapMon_imageRep` are isomorphisms: conjugation by an
isomorphism always is, and the internal-hom comparison is by
`CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.isIso_internalEndFunctorHom`, which is the only reason the two
categories are asked to be symmetric and `F` to be braided. -/
theorem isIso_mapMon_imageRep_iff [HasRightDual (image (leftMul C p))] :
    IsIso (F.mapMon.map (imageRep C p)) ↔
      IsIso (imageRep (F.mapMon.obj C) (mapPoint F p)) := by
  rw [← mapMon_imageRep F p, isIso_comp_right_iff]

end Dual

end CategoryTheory.Mon
